  </div>
  <p>
    The pay and routes for these are in <a href="/blog/career-options/career-in-psychology-india-salary-scope/">career in psychology in India: salary and scope</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="money">Money check before you pay for the clinical course</h2>
  <p>
    Our strongest suggestion is to keep the fee of a course or degree near a tenth of the money your family has set aside for education, and to read anything above a fifth as a signal to ask the course for proof. None of this applies to very cheap online learning. Free YouTube lessons and low-priced courses on Udemy or Coursera need little budget care, while the same subject sold as a university certificate can cost 30 to 100 times more.
  </p>
  <p>
    An illustration, not a real fee: with Rs 5 lakh set aside for all studies, a tenth is Rs 50,000 and a fifth is Rs 1,00,000. The rest pays for books, supervised practice, travel to interviews and living costs in the gap between contracts.
  </p>
  <p>
    Judge the specific course: is it recognised by the RCI, how many supervised clinical hours it gives, what past students went on to do, and what refund it allows. Free lectures can help you test the subject and prepare for entrance tests, but they do not replace a recognised clinical course, supervised training or registration.
  </p>

  <h2 id="checkpoint">Check before you commit: the four questions and the three proofs</h2>
  <p>
    The four questions tell you whether a government psychologist route fits your life, and the three proofs show you can actually do the job, so answer both before any course fee leaves your account.
  </p>

  <h3 id="four-questions">The four questions</h3>
  <div class="protocol">
    <div class="protocol-row">
      <div class="protocol-row__num">01</div>
      <div>
        <div class="protocol-row__title">Your fit: could you live this work daily?</div>
        <p>The job is case files, test scoring, written reports and long hours with people in distress. Spend a day with a working clinical psychologist before you pay for the course.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="protocol-row">
      <div class="protocol-row__num">02</div>
      <div>
        <div class="protocol-row__title">Your situation: can your family carry the wait?</div>
        <p>The road runs from a master's, to a clinical course, to a notice that may not come this year. Many first posts are fixed-amount contracts of Rs 25,000 to Rs 50,000, so work out how many months of gap you can cover.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="protocol-row">
      <div class="protocol-row__num">03</div>
      <div>
        <div class="protocol-row__title">Job market: are posts actually opening?</div>
        <p>Open the last few notices of the employer you want and count. Kerala PSC listed one post, and DRDO's 2022 notice listed 20 for the whole country.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="protocol-row">
      <div class="protocol-row__num">04</div>
      <div>
        <div class="protocol-row__title">AI-proof: what stays yours?</div>
        <p>Assessment judgement, therapy and the signed report stay with a registered person. Drafting and summaries can use AI help inside your hospital's data rules.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3 id="three-proofs">The three proofs</h3>
  <div class="gates-block">
    <div class="gates-row">
      <div class="gate">
        <span class="gate__num">Proof 1</span>
        <span class="gate__name">Show it</span>
        <p>Keep an anonymised practicum log and one assessment report written from a supervised case.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate">
        <span class="gate__num">Proof 2</span>
        <span class="gate__name">Say it</span>
        <p>Explain one assessment result, and what it cannot tell you, to a non-psychologist in 30 seconds to 2 minutes without notes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate">
        <span class="gate__num">Proof 3</span>
        <span class="gate__name">Get it checked</span>
        <p>Show your report to a supervising clinical psychologist, a psychiatrist and a senior colleague, and ask if they would rely on it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="mistakes">Expensive mistakes with government psychologist pay</h2>
  <div class="mistake-list">
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">01</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Comparing basic pay with another job's take-home pay</div>
        <p>Basic pay is only the start. Add DA and, on a regular post, HRA, then subtract deductions, before you set it beside a private offer.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">02</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Reading a consolidated contract figure as a pay scale</div>
        <p>A contract of Rs 40,000 has no scale, no promised DA and a short term. Ask what happens when the term ends.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">03</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Joining a clinical course without checking RCI recognition</div>
        <p>A course the RCI does not recognise can close the clinical posts. Check the RCI list and the rule for your intake year first.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">04</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Waiting for one notice with nothing else running</div>
        <p>Notices are irregular. Keep a paid counselling or training job going, so a missed notice does not stop your income and your proof. GATE (XH) or NET preparation also keeps teaching and research doors open.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mistake">
      <div class="mistake__num">05</div>
      <div>
        <div class="mistake__title">Paying anyone for a post</div>
        <p>Apply only on the employer's official recruitment website. No agent can sell you a government post.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="next-step">What to do next</h2>
  <p>
    Pick one post from the table, read its newest notice from first line to last, and write down the pay line, the qualification and the number of posts. Then note which proof you could build while you wait.
  </p>

  <p><strong>Try it now:</strong> <a href="/tools/education-cost-payback-planner/">Use the free education cost and payback planner</a> to set the cost of the clinical course and the months without pay against a fixed contract salary like the ones above.</p>

  <p>
    New psychologist notices appear on rac.gov.in for DRDO and the armed forces boards, on the recruitment pages of AIIMS campuses and NIMHANS, and on state health mission and public service commission sites.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you want a second view on whether to wait for a notice, train, or build a practice, <a href="/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/career-counselling-for-government-jobs/">career counselling for government jobs</a> is the place to begin. The aim is to make the decisions that unlock high income opportunities, build a high-income skill portfolio beside the post, and move toward earlier financial freedom.
  </p>
  <p>
    Related guides: <a href="/blog/government-jobs/state-vs-central-government-jobs-india/">state vs central government jobs</a>, <a href="/blog/skills/skills-required-for-psychology-careers-india/">skills required for psychology careers</a> and <a href="/blog/government-jobs/government-exam-preparation-while-working-india/">government exam preparation while working</a>.
  </p>
  <p class="note-line">
    Pay and post counts change with every new notice, so take final figures from the employer's own site.
  </p>

